{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b2f4c1a7-5d6e-4a1b-9c3f-freightid-tai-001",
    "name": "FreightID ← TAI Inbound Webhooks",
    "description": "Simulates TAI's inbound webhook deliveries for use cases 1 and 2.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Start the app: `npm run dev`\n2. Fill in the credential variables to match your `.env`. Set EITHER:\n   - `taiBasicUser` + `taiBasicPassword` (mirrors `TAI_WEBHOOK_BASIC_USER` / `_PASSWORD`), or\n   - `taiWebhookAuth` (mirrors `TAI_WEBHOOK_AUTH_TOKEN` — the whole string, `Bearer ` included).\n\n**Basic wins when both are set** — findings §3, and the server applies the same precedence. So if Basic vars are present in `.env`, a static Bearer token is ignored and comes back 401. The collection's pre-request script resolves the header the same way, keeping the two in sync.\n\n**What to expect**\nEvery request returns 200 except the deliberate 401. That is by design: TAI never re-sends a delivery, so rejecting a bad payload would destroy the event. Failures are recorded in the `webhook_events` table instead — check `processing_status` and `error` there.\n\nInspect results with `npm run db:studio`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "taiWebhookAuth",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "taiBasicUser",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "taiBasicPassword",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Resolves the Authorization header the way the server does:",
          "// Basic wins when both schemes are configured (findings §3).",
          "const user = pm.collectionVariables.get('taiBasicUser');",
          "const password = pm.collectionVariables.get('taiBasicPassword');",
          "",
          "if (user && password) {",
          "    const CryptoJS = require('crypto-js');",
          "    const encoded = CryptoJS.enc.Base64.stringify(",
          "        CryptoJS.enc.Utf8.parse(user + ':' + password)",
          "    );",
          "    pm.variables.set('resolvedAuth', 'Basic ' + encoded);",
          "} else {",
          "    pm.variables.set('resolvedAuth', pm.collectionVariables.get('taiWebhookAuth') || '');",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
